AB  -  INTERVENTION: Intervention 1: Intervention group: Patients in this group will receive a daily 10 mg tablet of empagliflozin (brand name: Gloripa), manufactured by Abidi Pharmaceutical Company. Administration begins 48 hours prior to coronary artery bypass graft surgery and continues for up to 72 hours postoperatively. The drug will be taken orally once daily, with water, regardless of meals. The total duration of treatment will be approximately 5 to 6 days. Intervention 2: Control group: Patients in this group will receive standard postoperative care after coronary artery bypass graft surgery along with a placebo identical in shape, size, and color to the active drug. The placebo, also produced by Abidi, will be administered orally once daily, following the same schedule as the intervention group (from 48 hours before to 72 hours after surgery). CONDITION: atrial fibrillation (AF). ; atrial fibrillation (AF) PRIMARY OUTCOME: The primary outcome variable in this study is the occurrence of atrial fibrillation (AF) after coronary artery bypass graft surgery (CABG). This variable is identified and documented by a cardiologist based on electrocardiographic (ECG) evidence and recorded episodes of atrial fibrillation within 48 to 72 hours postoperatively. Timepoint: Atrial fibrillation will be measured and recorded at the following time points:Before coronary artery bypass graft surgery (as baseline)48 hours after surgery72 hours after surgery. Method of measurement: Atrial fibrillation will be measured using a standard twelve‐lead electrocardiogram device at the specified time points. Final diagnosis will be made by a cardiologist based on electrocardiogram interpretation. INCLUSION CRITERIA: Patients aged 18 to 70 years who are candidates for coronary artery bypass graft surgery (coronary artery bypass grafting; CABG).
